<title>SINGAPORE: Central Properties half year up 27.3 pct.</title>
<headline>Central Properties half year up 27.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>	   (in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		13.28    vs    10.43</p>
<p>    Group share (cts)     44.30    vs    34.80</p>
<p>    Dividend (pct)	  30.00    vs    30.00</p>
<p>    Turnover		  13.53    vs     6.09</p>
<p>    Investment income     13.50    vs     6.05</p>
<p>    Interest expense	 1.45    vs     1.27</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit	   7.01    vs     4.62</p>
<p>    Associates		11.11    vs     9.52</p>
<p>    Tax			  4.85    vs     3.70</p>
<p>Last day books open - August 14, 1997</p>
<p>    Dividend pay	  - August 27, 1997</p>
<p>Note - Property and investment company, Central Properties Ltd said the higher pre-tax profit was due to an increase in dividend income mainly from long term investments and a 16.8 percent increase in the group's share of profits from associates. The higher turnover included S$5 million from the sales of short-term investments.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
